      "body": "## Problem\n\nThe paged selector in `qsa_select_decode_paged_forward` runs the deterministic FP32 `IndexerTopK`. On SM120, `IndexerTopK` serves at most `_SM120_DETERMINISTIC_MAX_NUM_COLS[torch.float32]` columns, which is 16,384, and its `check_support()` declines wider rows:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: deterministic IndexerTopK on SM120 supports at most 16384 columns for torch.float32, got 32768\n```\n\nThe `n_blocks_max=32768` cells in `test/python/gated_attention_block/cutedsl/test_qsa_score_paged.py` hit that decline, so on an RTX 5060 Ti (cc 12.0) they fail instead of skipping:\n- `test_paged_selection_matches_the_fp64_topk_set_up_to_ties`: 12 cells\n- `test_paged_selection_on_the_e4m3_pair_is_the_selection_on_the_same_values_upcast`: 3 cells\n\n## Change\n\nBoth tests skip those cells on SM120. The skip reads the cap from `indexer_top_k.api` and uses the API's own `(12, 0)` condition, so it follows any change to the cap. No other cell is affected.\n\n## Testing\n\nRTX 5060 Ti (cc 12.0), develop `a0f7b9f4`, cuDNN 9.27, `-m L0 test/python/gated_attention_block/cutedsl/test_qsa_score_paged.py`:\n- develop: 15 failed, 224 passed.\n- this PR: 0 failed, 224 passed, 17 skipped.\n\nI compared the outcomes test by test: every cell that passes on develop still passes.\n\n`black 26.3.1 --line-length 160 --fast` is clean.\n",
